          "text": "Reported episodes of low blood sugar symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For the past few weeks to possibly longer, episodes a few times per week, especially late morning on work days when breaks are skipped. Symptoms reported: shakiness, sweating, palpitations, hunger, dizziness, decreased concentration, and feeling 'funny in the head'. Episodes settle after juice or lollies. Hypoglycaemia is not objectively confirmed in the note."
      }
